<h2>Endorean Loot Rules:</h2>
<font size=2>
<ol seqnum=1>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Raid Points</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>For every raid that you attend you will receive a set number of
points.
    <li>In general, these will range from .1 to 2.5 points per raid.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>On Time</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>You will also receive .1 point for arriving to the zone of the first
raid of the night on time.
    <li>Our raids generally start at 8pm EST during the week and 3pm EST on
Weekends.
    <li>A posting in the member's section will list all raid start times.
    <li>Please login early enough before these times to get to whichever
target we may be hitting.
    <li>Porting classes will be awarded this bonus if they are online and
available to port at least 10 minutes prior to the scheduled start time.
    <li>Porting classes will also receive this bonus if they are in-zone
prior to the start of the raid and are asked to port others.
    <li>You will always have 30 minutes to get to a zone from the time it is
announced should we still be checking mobs at raid start time.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Item eligibility</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Item eligibility will be governed by the Loot Council members
present.
    <li>What this means is that Loot Council will determine the classes able
to bid on all items.
    <li>In most cases this is whatever classes can use said item. But, there
will be cases where bidding on an item will be restricted to a certain class
or two prior to being able to purchased by another class.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Bidding</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>When a mob dies, an Loot Council member or Raid Leader will ask
those attending who wants each item along with the point value for each
item.
    <li>Those who wish the item will give this person a tell and will place
their name in the lotto for the item.
    <li>The person with the most current points will win that item and the
points for the item will be deducted from that person's total current
points.
    <li>In the event of a tie, the person with the person with the most
Lifetime Points will be awarded the item.
    <li>In the event of a tie of Lifetime Points, a /random 500 will be done
between the individuals and whomever scores highest will get to purchase the
item.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Going Negative</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Going 'negative' will only be allowed per a Loot Council call on a
item.
    <li>And only if no other member is present who has the points and wishes
to purchase the item.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>No Cost Items</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>There will be items that do not require points to obtain.
    <li>Epic Raids, 10th Rings and 8th Shawls are not biddable items.
    <li>The other items that fall during these raids will have point values.

    <li>Additionally, some items will be set at a 0 point value due to their
plentiful supply or inherent stats/usability.
    <li>To determine who receives one of these items the guild will simply
look at those who need the item and compare Lifetime Points (not current
points).
    <li>Whomever has the most Lifetime Points will receive said item.
    <li>This rule is only in effect if this is designated as a guild raid.
    <li>Individual groups to obtain these items will retain their latitude
to determine who receives the item.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Assigned Items</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Sleeper's Tomb Keys and Emperor Key Parts will be assigned by the
Loot Council.
    <li>All primals that drop at Sleeper's Tomb raids will be assigned by
the Loot Council.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Partial Points</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>All raids will have a published point value for attendance.
    <li>To receive these points you must be present at the time the mob is
killed and actively participate in killing the mob.
    <li>Should you need to leave a raid prior to the mob being killed you
may make a request of the Loot Council member or Raid Leader of said raid
for partial points.
    <li>These will be handled on a case-by-case basis.
    <li>Some raids will also have built-in point values for this case setup
in advance. (Clearing the Plane of Growth, for example...a long process that
people may need to leave and come back during.)
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Point Values</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>All items will have a published point value.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Upgrade/Unwanted Items</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Should there be only one person at a raid who can use an item, or it
is a minor upgrade for multiple people who aren't willing to spend the
required full points for the item, the points required for purchasing said
item will be reduced to half.
    <li>Should noone still want to pay for that item then the item can be
purchased at full points for a twink (if they can get there in time) or the
item will simply rot.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Droppable Items</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Droppable items will be looted by a Loot Council member.
    <li>Should noone at the raid wish to pay for this item it will be made
available for full point purchase to those not at the raid for other mains.
    <li>Should no mains wish to purchase an item, a main may use their
points to purchase an item for a twink.
    <li>Should noone wish to purchase the item it will be placed up for sale
for our guild bank.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Item Turnin</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Should you purchase an upgrade for a slot where you have droppable
loot, you must turn in your current loot to the Loot Council for .5 x it's
current point value.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Discretionary points</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Discretionary points may be assigned by the Guild Leader.
    <li>These will be handled on a case-by-case basis and are reserved for
special incentives as determined by the officers.
    <li>This includes all Non-Raid incentives that will be achievable by
anyone in the guild who wishes to put the time and effort into the specific
task.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Endorean Firsts</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>The first time Endorean kills a mob the points awarded will be
doubled.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Raid cutoff points</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Raid cutoff points (in terms of numbers and classes) will be at the
sole descretion of the Raid Leader.
    <li>These will be processed on a first-come first served basis.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Minimum Level</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Your character must reach level 57 before you are eligible to begin
accumulating points and spending them on items that drop at raids.
    <li>All characters will be considered main characters after they reach
this level and will accrue points according to their raid attendance.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Multiple Characters</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>At the discretion of the Raid Leader, multiple characters may be
played by the same individual at the raid.
    <li>You must have permission from the Raid Leader to bring a secondary
character.
    <li>The main character will receive full point value for the mob kill.
    <li>A second character owned by the main and requested to come kill a
mob will receive .5 the point value for the mob kill.
    <li>A secondary character who is a main of someone who is not present
will receive .25 the point value for the mob kill.
    <li>Only one secondary will count for purposes of point accruals.
    <li>Should people wish to play a secondary that is not requested, but
permitted by the Raid Leader, the secondary character will receive no points
for the raid. Lastly, should you be requested by the Raid Leader to play a
alternate main as your only character on the raid you may contact the LC
member on the raid and request that the points for that raid be allocated to
your main character instead of your alternate main.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Raid Recording</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>All people present at the raid are required to be un-anon.
    <li>This is done for recording purposes.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Deguilding</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>If you deguild from the guild your point totals (Lifetime, Spent,
Current) are reset to 0.
    <li>Should you be re-admitted to the guild you will earn points as a new
member would.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Applicants</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Applicants will not earn points.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>New members</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>New members will accrue points according to their attendance.
    <li>There is a one month waiting period from the time you join the guild
till you can spend your points as a full member.
    <li>New members during this period will not be allowed to bid on items
unless the item is no_drop and would otherwise rot.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Changing Point Values</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Due to the ever-changing nature of loot, the Loot Council reserves
the right to change loot point values at any time.
    <li>This includes doing so at raids for whatever purpose.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Deflation</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>Deflation is part of the system.
    <li>On a periodic basis, determined by the officers, the entire group of
people with positive Current point totals will experience a straight-line
percentage decrease in point totals.
    <li>This will be an across the board cut in total current points
designed to make sure that the system is in balance appropriately.
    <li>These will be announced ahead of time.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>Point Errors</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>It is the responsibility of the individual members to make sure that
the point values recorded for their participation is correct.
    <li>Any issues with this should be registered with the raid leader or
Loot Council member present at the raid in question.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
<li><b><u><font color=white>System Changes</font></u></b>
    <ol seqnum=1>
    <font size=-1>
    <li>The leadership of Endorean understands that over time changes to
this system are inevitable.
    <li>We will adjust it as necessary and reserve the right to change our
system at a future date.
    </font>
    </ol>
</li>
<br>
</ol>

</font>
